.113725 .141176 .129412 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 56 360.5 Tm /F4+0 10 Tf 12 TL (1.1 Explain Scrum as Teams using agility to develop Products in a complex environment.) Tj T* ET
.113725 .141176 .129412 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 56 347.5 Tm /F4+0 10 Tf 12 TL (1.2 Describe the Scrum Team as a small, indivisible group that produces Results for Stakeholders.) Tj T* ET
.113725 .141176 .129412 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 56 334.5 Tm /F4+0 10 Tf 12 TL (1.3 Distinguish Product Owner value accountability from Scrum Master improvement work.) Tj T* ET
.113725 .141176 .129412 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 56 321.5 Tm /F4+0 10 Tf 12 TL (1.4 Explain how the Product Owner orders the Backlog toward a Product Goal.) Tj T* ET
.113725 .141176 .129412 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 56 308.5 Tm /F4+0 10 Tf 12 TL (1.5 Describe Sprint Planning as agreeing a Sprint Goal and a Sprint Backlog.) Tj T* ET
.113725 .141176 .129412 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 56 295.5 Tm /F4+0 10 Tf 12 TL (1.6 Contrast a Product Owner canceling a Sprint with a Scrum Master Abnormal Termination.) Tj T* ET
.113725 .141176 .129412 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 56 282.5 Tm /F4+0 10 Tf 12 TL (1.7 Outline the Product Review and Team Retrospective that end a Sprint.) Tj T* ET
